From 5b00a86fb4f71a9e8792dc2efda7318187a3c5c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Mostovoy <stavultras@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:22:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hw/mips: MediaTek MT7621 router machine (mt7621-router)

MIPS 1004Kc CPU model, CM GCR coherence registers, a settable GIC timer
frequency and a CACHE instruction hook for boards (the MT7621 TPL runs
the SPL from L2 cache locked as SRAM); the mt7621-router machine with
DRAM wrap-around, palmbus register file with the DDR init blob's status
bits, Frame Engine PSE SRAM, SPI controller (more-buffer mode) with the
Filogic SPI-NOR model memory-mapped at the reset vector, UART, and the
Filogic Ethernet model with NETSYS v1 QDMA descriptors, configurable
PDMA/QDMA bases and an MT7530 switch (MCM) for MT7621.
